# Example age calibrations for the synthetic data in this directory.
#
# The three ages below are USER INPUT for this example.  Delphy has no built-in human mtDNA ages;
# the names root / M / N are labels for sample sets, and nothing in Delphy knows what they mean.
# "taxa all" is the MRCA of the SAMPLED lineages, which is the root of the supplied tree -- not by
# itself the common ancestor of all human mtDNA.
version 1

calibration root
  taxa all
  age_units ka
  age_reference_year 1950
  distribution lognormal
  median 140
  sigma 0.15
  oldest 400
  youngest 60
end

calibration M
  taxa SAMPLE_A SAMPLE_B SAMPLE_C SAMPLE_D SAMPLE_E
  age_units ka
  age_reference_year 1950
  distribution normal
  mean 100
  stddev 12
end

calibration N
  taxa SAMPLE_A SAMPLE_B SAMPLE_C
  age_units cal_bp
  distribution uniform
  oldest 75000
  youngest 45000
end
